{"kind":"propose","text":"Reject non-canonical authority targets before they can become misleading durable acts. Ratify, supersede, and merge approval inputs must be full canonical same-workroom event identifiers; a bare digest or foreign-workroom identifier is an input error, never something to auto-expand or append ineffectively. MCP summaries must report the projected verdict and reason, so an appended ineffective act cannot be described as successful.","body":{"conditions":"Use one shared validator at the application boundary before signing ratify or supersede requests, and apply the same contract to gs merge --approval before receipt reservation, checkout mutation, or durable append. Reject rather than canonicalize ambiguous bare digests. Preserve valid canonical behavior and idempotent replay. Update the affected CLI, MCP, and reference documentation. Add mutation-sensitive app, CLI, and MCP regressions proving malformed or foreign targets leave the sequence frontier, checkout HEAD, and merge receipt refs unchanged, and proving ineffective projected results are never summarized as ok. Publish exact-head per-path artifacts and obtain independent review with Architecture, Security, and Simplification conclusions."}}